//!   its references written out as dtc resolves them (`<&gic>` is phandle 1, which dtc gives
//!   the node it adds a `phandle` property to; `&uart0` in `/aliases` is the path
//!   `"/serial@0"`), instead of being assembled from dtc's output. dtc's layout is kept: the
//!   header, the empty memory reservation map at 0x28, the structure block, the strings in
//!   the order of their first use (no suffix merging), then the 16384 bytes of padding
//!   (`-p 16384`). The reference test (`just test-ref`) compares the bytes with
//!   `dt_blob.S`. The labels `dt_header`, `gic`, `uart0`... which nothing reads, are not
//!   defined.

